# Data Sync, Storage, Crypto & Security

**Scope:** All backend, database, local cache, encryption, realtime sync, push notification, and logging layers — regardless of stack (**Supabase, Firebase, REST, GraphQL, gRPC, WebSockets, PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, SQLite, Drift, Hive, Isar, IndexedDB**). Wins over other rules for sync, encryption, and notification hot paths.

---

## 1) Backend, Database & Config Abstraction (Any Backend / Any DB)

- **Repository / Service encapsulation:** Isolate all remote API and database operations behind instance-based services/repositories (`*_service` / `*_repository`) exposing typed models (`fromJson`/`toJson`/`copyWith`) and throwing typed **`AppException`**.
- **Centralized configuration:** Load all API URLs, database endpoints, and public keys strictly from centralized config/environment modules (`appConfig`, `.env*`) — **never** hardcode URLs, tokens, or credentials, and **never** ship admin/service-role keys in client code or repositories.
- **Versioned migrations:** Track all database schema, index, trigger, and security policy (RLS/RBAC) changes in versioned migration files as a single source of truth shared across clients.
- **Zero secret logging:** **NEVER** log auth tokens, passwords, OTPs, message/content plaintext, or private encryption keys.
- **Production release signing:** Ship mobile release builds exclusively with configured release signing (`android/key.properties`, release certificates) — never debug signing.

### Service Pattern

```dart
class FeatureService {
  FeatureService(this._client);

  final BackendClient _client;

  Future<ResultModel> fetchItem(String id) async {
    try {
      final data = await _client.getById(id);
      return ResultModel.fromJson(data);
    } catch (e) {
      throw AppException('Failed to fetch item: $e');
    }
  }
}
```

